    "title": "Bridgit Mendler Says Surprise EP Drop Wasn't Her: 'When It Is, Trust Me, You'll Know' - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Maddy Lennon ,\n3 hours ago\nBridgit Mendler did not make her return to music like fans thought.\nSix new songs apparently from the former Disney star appeared on her Spotify and Apple Music pages on Friday (June 5). The songs included “Loyalties,” “Oxygen,” “Mercy,” “Long Run,” “Cold,” and “Flowers,” and appeared to be an exciting new EP.\nUnfortunately, the 33-year-old took to her X account on Wednesday (June 10) to share that she was not behind the surprise drop.\n“Sorry to disappoint everyone, the spotify release wasn’t me!” she wrote. She then added a follow-up tweet saying, “When it is, trust me, you’ll know.”\nBridgit left Hollywood almost ten years ago to pursue a career in the tech space and hasn’t officially released new music since\nIn case you missed it, back in March, Bridgit actually spoke about how her time at Disney helped shape her and assisted with her later endeavors such as her tech career.\n“It was a great time in my life… super formative experience,” Bridgit tells The Free Press . “I started that show when I was 17, and continued on for 100 episodes. So it was a rigorous time in life.”\n“There were times when, you know, I would be filming a TV show… 12 hours each day during the week, and then going to the studio after, and then doing concerts on the weekends,” she continued. Read the rest of what she said here !\nThe post appeared first on .",
    "summary": "Bridgit Mendler did not make her return to music like fans thought. Six new songs apparently from the former Disney star appeared on her Spotify and Apple Music pages on Friday (June 5). The songs included “Loyalties,” “Oxygen,” “Mercy,” “Long Run,” “Cold,” and “Flowers,” and appeared to be an exciting new EP.",
